Written to `ADR-001-notification-architecture.md`.

**Recommendation:** Redis Streams. The decision hinges on three decisive constraints — existing Redis infrastructure (zero new ops), team size with no Kafka experience (steep learning curve would consume 25% of the team for weeks), and the 2-week delivery target (unreachable with Kafka). Redis Streams handles 10x traffic at ~15% of a single-node Redis capacity, consumer groups map directly to the worker pool pattern, and exactly-once for billing is achieved through consumer-side idempotency (stream entry ID + PostgreSQL dedup table) rather than broker-side transactions.

The ADR evaluates Kafka, SQS/SNS, and PostgreSQL LISTEN/NOTIFY as alternatives, each with a concrete rejection rationale tied to the team's constraints — and a clear threshold for when Kafka becomes the right choice (>100k events/s, event sourcing need, or dedicated platform team).
